-# locals: captions (Array) — the Work's caption Blobs, one per language, for
-# the list of current files. removed (Array, optional) — withdrawn caption
-# assets, each carrying its `file_set`. removable (Boolean, optional) — offer
-# Remove and Restore, which submit the empty remove-caption and
-# restore-caption forms outside the metadata form.
-#
-# Offered only for a Work with audio or video content: CaptionTrack.applicable?
-# on the edit page, StagedMediaProbe at deposit, where the Blob may still be in flight.
-#
-# The fields ride the surrounding metadata form (multipart on both pages) rather
-# than owning a form of its own, because a nested <form> is stripped by the
-# browser and a sibling one would need its own page — the depositor would lose
-# unsaved metadata to reach it.
-#
-# The names are bare (`caption`, `caption_language`), not `work[caption]`: this
-# is a file the controller stages and hands to a job, not an Atlas metadata
-# field, which is the same reason the Thumbnail input beside it is bare too.
%hr.section-divider.my-3

.my-3.rounded-3
  %h4.pb-2
    %i.fa-solid.fa-closed-captioning.me-2{ 'aria-hidden' => 'true' }
    Captions

  - if captions.any?
    %ul.caption-tracks.list-unstyled.mb-3{ 'aria-label' => 'Current caption files' }
      - captions.each do |caption|
        - label = CaptionTrack.label(caption)
        %li.caption-tracks__row
          %span.caption-tracks__label{ lang: CaptionTrack.language(caption) }= label
          %span.caption-tracks__tag= CaptionTrack.language(caption)
          %span.caption-tracks__actions
            = link_to 'View', media_path(caption.noid), class: 'btn btn-tonal-secondary btn-sm',
                      'aria-label' => "View the #{label} caption file"
            - if local_assigns[:removable]
              %button.btn.btn-tonal-danger.btn-sm{ type: 'submit', form: 'remove-caption', name: 'caption_id', value: caption.noid,
                'aria-label' => "Remove the #{label} caption file",
                data: { turbo_confirm: "Remove the #{label} caption file? It leaves the player and the downloads, and can be restored from this page.",
                        turbo_confirm_title: 'Remove caption file', turbo_confirm_button: 'Remove',
                        turbo_confirm_variant: 'danger' } }
                %i.fa-solid.fa-trash-can.me-1{ 'aria-hidden' => 'true' }
                Remove

  - removed = Array(local_assigns[:removed])
  - if local_assigns[:removable] && removed.any?
    %h5.caption-tracks__heading Removed caption files
    %ul.caption-tracks.caption-tracks--removed.list-unstyled.mb-3{ 'aria-label' => 'Removed caption files' }
      - removed.each do |caption|
        - label = CaptionTrack.label(caption)
        %li.caption-tracks__row
          %span.caption-tracks__label{ lang: CaptionTrack.language(caption) }= label
          %span.caption-tracks__tag= CaptionTrack.language(caption)
          %span.caption-tracks__meta
            Removed #{file_version_when(caption[:tombstoned_at])} by #{file_version_who(caption[:tombstoned_by])}
          %span.caption-tracks__actions
            %button.btn.btn-tonal-primary.btn-sm{ type: 'submit', form: 'restore-caption', name: 'file_set_id', value: caption.file_set,
              'aria-label' => "Restore the #{label} caption file" }
              %i.fa-solid.fa-rotate-left.me-1{ 'aria-hidden' => 'true' }
              Restore

  .row.g-2{ data: { controller: 'caption-language' } }
    .col-md-7
      %label.form-label{ for: 'caption' } Caption file
      %input#caption.form-control{ name: 'caption', type: 'file', accept: CaptionTrack::EXTENSION }/
    .col-md-5
      %label.form-label{ for: 'caption_language' } Language
      %select#caption_language.form-select{ name: 'caption_language',
                                             data: { action: 'caption-language#toggle', 'caption-language-target': 'select' } }
        - CaptionTrack::LANGUAGES.each do |tag, english, own|
          %option{ value: tag }= english == own ? english : "#{english} — #{own}"
        %option{ value: CaptionTrack::OTHER } Other…
    .col-md-5.offset-md-7{ hidden: true, data: { 'caption-language-target': 'other' } }
      .row.g-2
        .col-5
          %label.form-label.small{ for: 'caption_language_tag' } Language tag
          %input#caption_language_tag.form-control.form-control-sm{ name: 'caption_language_tag', placeholder: 'es-MX',
                                                                     autocomplete: 'off', spellcheck: 'false' }/
        .col-7
          %label.form-label.small{ for: 'caption_language_label' } Label in the player
          %input#caption_language_label.form-control.form-control-sm{ name: 'caption_language_label', placeholder: 'Español (México)',
                                                                       maxlength: CaptionTrack::LABEL_LIMIT }/
  %p.text-muted.small.mt-2.mb-0
    Caption files must be in WebVTT (.vtt) format. Contact repository staff for help converting caption files to WebVTT.
    Uploading a file in a language this work already has replaces that language's file, and the earlier one is kept in its version history.

%hr.section-divider.mt-3.mb-0
